        "Tax-deferred savings generally provide tax savings now and postpone tax payments until later.",
        "Traditional IRAs and 401(k) accounts are commonly described as tax-deferred savings accounts.",
        "Roth IRA earnings are generally tax-free rather than tax-deferred when distributions are qualified.",
        "Roth IRA distributions are generally qualified after age 59.5, subject to exceptions.",
        "Earnings from nonqualified Roth IRA distributions may be taxed.",
        "Earnings from nonqualified Roth IRA distributions may incur a 10% penalty.",
        "The answer attributes the information about tax treatment and distributions to page 1."
    ]
}
